From fe07651aa9b1af50aa6f441a8503060e146777ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): replace runtime custody hook with reviewed
 static inventory [daveey]

Decision B removes the SQLite authorizer, its autouse fixture, and every
hook-only regression. Preserve the reviewed mutation classifications and pin
exact module-qualified function, verb and table identities in a static test.
Qualify Journal._initialize and History.record as class methods; AST-check
exact declarations rather than accepting suffix or substring matches.

Known gap: this snapshot cannot discover unlisted writers or prove that a
listed function body still writes exactly the declared tables. This is a
reviewed explicit list, not completeness certification or runtime enforcement.
No spec change, deployment, activation, row stamping or certification.

Proof: focused inventory suite passes (4 tests). Full check hit a stale-base
health cap in untouched gateway/run.py; rebase and rerun before publication.
---
